BROWSER COMPONENTS LOADED AT RUNTIME FROM A CDN

  These are not listed in package.json and will be missed by an SBOM tool
  pointed only at the manifest. They are fetched by the browser at page load.

  @simplewebauthn/browser    10.0.0    MIT
                                       vendored inline in src/locked.html
  Google Identity Services   n/a       Proprietary — Google Terms of Service
                                       https://accounts.google.com/gsi/client
                                       loaded by the OAuth consent page
                                       generated in src/mcp-oauth.ts

  2026-08-14: src/gate.html is deleted along with the three routes that served it,
  and the two entries that named it as their only loader went with it. qrcodejs is
  no longer fetched anywhere in this tree. @simplewebauthn/browser is no longer
  fetched from a CDN either -- src/locked.html carries it inline, pinned by tarball
  sha512 and file sha384, so the Subresource Integrity finding below no longer
  applies to it.

  KNOWN ISSUE: the Google Identity Services script is loaded from a CDN without a
  Subresource Integrity hash. Google does not publish a stable hash for it, so this
  is tracked as a security finding rather than fixed. See SECURITY.md.

